1019	  # c1 holds t1 and has written. The grantor's messages to c2 are dropped (c2 still
1020	  # reaches the grantor, and everyone else is untouched). c2 requests; the grantor
1021	  # records Grant(c2, t2) and the message is lost. On that Grant event the grantor
1022	  # crashes and never restarts. After this last fault the two remaining lease nodes,
1023	  # storage and c2 are connected to each other both ways, so C1.4's premise holds
1024	  # (Rule L3): c2 must eventually hold a grant, with no further `request` step, and
1025	  # its token must exceed t2, a token that left the grantor's log and reached no one.
1026	  # c2's write waits for that token (Rule T3) and must be accepted with
1027	  # highest_before = t1; c1's stale read is then rejected (C2.1).
1028	  - {at: start, do: {request: c1}}
1029	  - {at: {event: Grant, client: c1}, do: {write: c1, value: v1}}
1030	  - {at: {event: WriteAck, client: c1, outcome: accepted}, do: {cell: F2.2, drop: [[grantor, c2]]}}
1031	  - {at: start, do: {request: c2}}
1032	  - {at: {event: Grant, client: c2}, do: {cell: F1.1, crash: grantor}}
1033	  - {at: start, do: {write: c2, value: v2}}
1034	  - {at: {event: WriteAck, client: c2, outcome: accepted}, do: {read: c1, token: stale}}
1035	end: {event: ReadAck, client: c1}
