1046	  # After the first grant the direct link between the grantor and c2 is cut both
1047	  # ways and stays cut. Nothing else changes: the grantor still exchanges messages
1048	  # with both followers, so no election is provoked, and the two followers, storage
1049	  # and c2 are connected to each other both ways. Under Rule L3 that is exactly
1050	  # C1.4's premise (a majority of lease nodes, storage and the requester, connected
1051	  # to each other; the clause does not name the grantor), so c2 must eventually be
1052	  # granted even though it can never exchange a message with the current leader.
1053	  - {at: start, do: {request: c1}}
